r11 L1 step 1 (POST HOC, correlational): LPM-128 crossing analysis of the 24 committed 300k BURST runs

- analysis/lpm_crossing.py (python -m analysis.lpm_crossing): port of the r11 lpm scout's queue_vs_128 / crossing
  scripts over results/nova/r7_native_grid_vllm_pulled_20261025-145126 and e2_170933xx_pulled_20261025-144558.
  Stock LPM held its waiting queue above SGLang's WAITING_QUEUE_PREFIX_MATCH_MAX = 128 (schedule_policy.py :132-133,
  :300-311, md5 b8ec334a...) for >= 300 s in 5/12 runs, all 5 collapsed; 0/7 of the others did. Fisher one-sided
  p = 0.0013 (stratified by rate 0.011, one unit per stream 0.05); reverse causation shown directly by FCFS.
  Scheduler cost drops from about 0.011 to 0.003 s/s at the crossing.
